initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">3) Place the strike team =
policy levers below the graph on the simulator tab and for each lever we =
need to enable a year-by-year accounting methodology, because there is =
no way any particular lever can deliver a consistent amount of water as =
the source constantly changes.  e.g., ag optimization and leasing  will =
only work following good water years.  Like this year, the streams are =
dry but reservoirs still have banked water. So water rights may be =
diverted from storage systems to GSL.  But if the next year is also dry, =
that strategy is screwed.  Likewise, Newfoundland has water this year, =
but if we bring it back to the lake, then that is a one-time benefit.  =
Mineral extraction at USMag has ceased. so we are not drawing that water =
out.  But accounting wise, I guess we get to count it every year. =
Similarly phragmites...&nbsp;</span></div><div><br></div><div><span =
